From fb66a81c799d9595000abe06f14febff75ef2492 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Code Review <claude-review@example.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 08:37:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add username editing and basic abuse guardrails
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- profile.js: accept a name/username change alongside email/password,
  with the same validation pattern as the rest of that endpoint
- authOptions: refresh the JWT from the DB when the client calls
  session update() (used by the settings page after a save), so a
  new name/email shows up immediately instead of on next login
- settings.js: rewrite to actually edit name + email (prefilled from
  the session), keep optional password change, add sign-out
- dashboard.js: link to /settings, which was previously unreachable;
  show the user's name when set
- add src/lib/rateLimit.js, a small in-memory fixed-window limiter
  (documented limitation: per-process, not shared across serverless
  instances — fine to ship now, swap for Upstash Redis later if
  abuse becomes real)
- register.js: rate-limit by IP (5 / 15 min) to slow mass account
  creation
- qr/create.js: rate-limit by user (30 / hour) and cap active links
  per user at 50, so one account can't be used to spray the
  redirect endpoint with slugs
